@startuml
title CORE-10 — secure binding and delivery
actor User
participant "Next.js settings" as Web
participant "NestJS / TelegramModule" as API
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "Telegram Bot API" as Telegram
participant "Existing business services" as Business
participant "CORE-09 (backend pending)" as Events
User -> Web : authenticated cookie session
Web -> API : POST link + Origin
API -> DB : lock user, store SHA-256 token / 5 min
API --> Web : deep link (raw token returned once)
User -> Telegram : private /start token
Telegram -> API : HTTPS webhook + secret header
API -> DB : atomic receipt + token claim + outbox reply
User -> Web : refresh; verify Telegram account ID
Web -> API : confirm pending link
API -> DB : verify owner/expiry; unique chat; delete token
Business -> API : requestCreated / taskChanged(tx)
API -> DB : minimal message + recipients in business transaction
Events ..> API : publish(tx, stable event ID + authorized recipients)
API -> DB : conditional UPDATE PENDING to SENDING
API -> DB : recheck role, binding, subscription
API -> Telegram : protected minimal message
Telegram --> API : message_id / sanitized failure
API -> DB : SENT / PENDING(backoff) / FAILED / UNKNOWN
note over Events
No independent reminder scheduler.
Personal actions and overdue require CORE-09.
end note
@enduml
